{"id":"n-20261018-irw30p","category":"world","display_title":"Pope Discharged After Surgery","display_title_he":"האפיפיור שוחרר מבית החולים לאחר ניתוח","short_summary":"Pope Leo XIV has left Rome's Gemelli Hospital just days after undergoing surgery for lung cancer. He is expected to lead Sunday's prayer and maintain plans for future travel.","english_level":"C1","words":415,"reading_time":3,"image":null,"sources":[{"name":"BBC News","domain":"bbc.co.uk","url":"https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c5x2vkddrkrko","title":"Pope discharged from hospital days after lung cancer surgery","published_at":"2026-10-17T13:51:36.000Z"},{"name":"NPR","domain":"npr.org","url":"https://www.npr.org/2026/10/17/nx-s1-6006762/pope-leo-xiv-leaves-hospital-days-after-lung-cancer-surgery","title":"Pope Leo XIV leaves hospital days after lung cancer surgery","published_at":"2026-10-17T15:10:14.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-17T13:51:36.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-18T05:48:13.605Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":9,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["Pope Leo XIV has been discharged from Rome's Gemelli Hospital just days after undergoing a surgical procedure to remove the lower lobe of his right lung due to cancer. According to medical staff, including his personal physician Dr. Luigi Carbone and chief thoracic surgeon Professor Stefano Margaritora, the 71-year-old pontiff walked unaided to his waiting vehicle, pausing briefly to greet well-wishers outside the facility. Vatican officials reported that morning blood tests and chest X-rays confirmed a steady clinical improvement, allowing for an earlier-than-expected release after five days in the hospital. Medical experts examining the tissue confirmed a diagnosis of lung adenocarcinoma, though outside specialists noted that utilizing surgery as an initial tool strongly indicates the condition was caught at an early stage. Prior to his departure, the Pope celebrated Mass in a tenth-floor hospital room for staff members and distributed communion.","Despite the major operation, the Vatican announced that the Pope intends to lead the traditional Angelus prayer and blessing from the window of the papal apartment to crowds gathered in St. Peter's Square. While his public schedule remains completely cleared until October 20, preparations are still under consideration for an international trip to Latin America in early November, encompassing visits to Uruguay, Argentina, and Peru, where he lived for two decades and holds citizenship. Physicians and specialists observing his recovery pointed out that his robust baseline health, maintained through regular tennis and horse riding at Castel Gandolfo, contributes favorably to his postoperative outlook. Experts like Dr. Vin Gupta and Dr. Jonathan Villena Vargas noted that patients in good physical shape undergoing minimally invasive video-assisted surgery frequently recover quickly.","Amidst his medical recovery, diplomatic engagements continued. On Friday, the Pope spoke with Russian President Vladimir Putin for the first time since June 2025. According to the Vatican, the conversation focused on urging dialogue and peace amid the intensifying bombardment across Ukraine and growing civilian casualties. Furthermore, the pontiff appealed for an urgent humanitarian ceasefire in the Russian-occupied Ukrainian city of Oleshkiy to facilitate civilian evacuations and the delivery of essential food and medicine, noting reports of residents eating garden weeds to survive. The Pope also learned that his older brother Louis, living in Florida, had been hospitalized with a form of cancer, while his mother Mildred died of cancer in 1990. While top Vatican diplomats emphasize that the pontiff's health should never be taken for granted, his swift return to public duties has provided reassurance to Catholics worldwide who were initially surprised by the diagnosis announced last week."],"facts":[{"fact":"Pope Leo XIV was discharged from Rome's Gemelli Hospital four days after undergoing surgery to remove the lower lobe of his right lung due to lung adenocarcinoma.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"The 71-year-old Pope walked unaided to his car and is scheduled to lead the Angelus prayer on Sunday.","sources":[1,2]},{"fact":"Before leaving the hospital, the Pope spoke by phone with Russian President Vladimir Putin to urge dialogue and peace regarding Ukraine, and called for a humanitarian ceasefire in Oleshkiy.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Despite his cancer diagnosis and surgery, the Pope's schedule currently retains a planned November trip to Latin America, though further treatment or assessment remains possible.","sources":[1,2]}],"glossary":[{"text":"Pope","lemma":"pope","pos":"noun","he":"אפיפיור","name":"Pope Leo XIV"},{"text":"Leo","lemma":"Leo","pos":"noun","he":"לאו","name":"Pope Leo XIV"},{"text":"XIV","lemma":"XIV","pos":"number","he":"הארבעה עשר","name":null},{"text":"discharged","lemma":"discharge","pos":"verb","he":"שוחרר","name":null},{"text":"Rome's","lemma":"Rome","pos":"noun","he":"של רומא","name":"Gemelli Hospital"},{"text":"Gemelli","lemma":"Gemelli","pos":"noun","he":"ג'מלי","name":"Gemelli Hospital"},{"text":"Hospital","lemma":"hospital","pos":"noun","he":"בית חולים","name":"Gemelli Hospital"},{"text":"surgical","lemma":"surgical","pos":"adjective","he":"כירורגי","name":null},{"text":"procedure","lemma":"procedure","pos":"noun","he":"הליך","name":null},{"text":"remove","lemma":"remove","pos":"verb","he":"להסיר","name":null},{"text":"lower","lemma":"lower","pos":"adjective","he":"תחתון","name":null},{"text":"lobe","lemma":"lobe","pos":"noun","he":"אונה","name":null},{"text":"right","lemma":"right","pos":"adjective","he":"ימני","name":null},{"text":"lung","lemma":"lung","pos":"noun","he":"ריאה","name":null},{"text":"cancer","lemma":"cancer","pos":"noun","he":"סרטן","name":null},{"text":"medical","lemma":"medical","pos":"adjective","he":"רפואי","name":null},{"text":"staff","l